WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.440
If you are living in a black and white world,
where everything is either good or bad, with

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:11.800
no shades of gray, and you feel sad and empty
with an intense fear of being left alone — then

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:20.840
you might be experiencing what’s known as
BPD.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:26.280
Borderline Personality Disorder is a mental
health condition characterized by a distorted

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:32.400
self-image, along with difficulties regulating
emotions and maintaining relationships.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.320
It affects around 1-2% of all adults.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.920
Like all mental health disorders, it is considered
to be on a spectrum, meaning that it can manifest

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:53.080
in all sorts of ways, ranging from regular
outbursts of anger to severe forms of self-harm.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:59.080
The causes of BPD aren't fully understood,
also because it goes hand in hand with addiction,

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.840
other mental health issues and eating disorders.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:08.160
Environmental factors, such as a childhood
of neglect and abuse seem to play a role,—

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.120
but so may genetics.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:17.120
Since science has not yet been able to find
any biological evidence to diagnose mental

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:22.480
disorders, we have to turn to symptoms to
see if someone may have BPD.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.160
To illustrate this, meet Alex.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:33.120
Alex is a 20 year-old college boy who has
always been sensitive, but lately also feels

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.960
isolated and extremely emotional.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:42.760
He experiences five symptoms that are often
associated with the condition.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.960
Alex experiences rapid changes in self-identity.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.600
In a single day he can go from feeling godlike
to feeling worthless.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.400
And in a crisis, he changes from one personality
to another.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.360
This is when he goes through&nbsp;
moments of dissociation,&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.920
where he feels detached from his body — with

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.160
no sense of self at all.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:09.760
Alex has what’s known as a Distorted Self-Image.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:13.560
He experiences intense and unstable emotions.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:19.320
The smallest setbacks can send his mind spiraling
out of control and make him end friendships

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.040
in an instant.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.600
Every emotion he feels, he feels intensely.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.200
Joy becomes euphoria and sadness turns into
depression.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:37.000
This emotional rollercoaster leaves him exhausted
— that is when he dissociates.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.280
He struggles with Impulsiveness.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.600
When talking to his friends, Alex often feels
misunderstood.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:48.600
With close to no self-control, he starts shouting
or lashing out.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.600
Later, he feels ashamed.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:58.480
To cope, he eats, does drugs, or turns violent
— often against himself.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.560
He has an intense Fear of Abandonment.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.240
When his girlfriend cancels their date at
the last minute, he breaks up with her, and

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.040
a few minutes later bombards her with texts,
asking for forgiveness.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.640
He is constantly worried she will leave him,&nbsp;

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:19.440
and demands impossibly high&nbsp;
standards of reassurance.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.760
All of this leads to Unstable Relationships.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:28.200
When Alex fears he will be abandoned, he hurts
his friends for no obvious reason.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:33.280
By pushing others away he thinks he can avoid
being pushed away himself.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.600
He later feels ashamed and promises to change.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:44.040
After an intense period of paranoia, Alex
wants to drop out of college, which at this

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.960
point is pretty much the only stable thing
left in his life.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:53.640
It’s then that his best friend asks him
to seek help.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:59.040
When Alex speaks to a professional, he learns
about BPD and that the typical treatments

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:07.080
are forms of psychotherapy - like CBT - cognitive
behavioral therapy, DBT - dialectical-behavioral

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:13.760
therapy or MBT - mentalization based therapy.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:19.360
The psychiatrist also explains that in some
cases patients take medication, such as mood

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.800
stabilizers.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:26.880
This can be important as over 50% of adolescents
that attempt to take their lives are diagnosed

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.600
with borderline personality disorder.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:37.040
Understanding his condition is a relief — at
least he knows he’s not alone.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.280
What do you think?

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:41.600
What can we do to help people with BPD?

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:59.560
Please share your thoughts or your own experiences
with this condition in the comments below.

